  "comments": [
    {
      "paragraph_index": 2,
      "comment": ""
    },
    {
      "paragraph_index": 4,
      "comment": "pH to 7.0 with KOH"
    },
    {
      "paragraph_index": 5,
      "comment": ""
    },
    {
      "paragraph_index": 6,
      "comment": "The medium was purged with N2 and dispensed inside an anaerobic chamber into 27-ml crimp-top tubes (Bellco, Vineland, N.J.)."
    },
    {
      "paragraph_index": 7,
      "comment": "The tubes were then sealed with aluminum-crimp Teflon-coated butyl rubber stoppers (Wheaton, Millville, N.J.) and autoclaved at 121oC for 55 min."
    },
    {
      "paragraph_index": 8,
      "comment": "The tube headspaces were flushed with sterile 70% N2–30% CO2 (Matheson Gas Products, Inc., Secaucus, N.J.) and received the following sterile and anaerobic additions before inoculation (final medium volume, ~10 ml per tube):"
    },
    {
      "paragraph_index": 10,
      "comment": ""
    },
    {
      "paragraph_index": 12,
      "comment": ""
    },
    {
      "paragraph_index": 13,
      "comment": "Anaerobic digestor sludge supernatant (SS):"
    },
    {
      "paragraph_index": 14,
      "comment": "The anaerobic sewage digestor sludge for preparation of SS was obtained from the Ithaca Area Wastewater Treatment Facility."
    },
    {
      "paragraph_index": 15,
      "comment": "Several liters were collected at one time, to ensure uniformity."
    },
    {
      "paragraph_index": 16,
      "comment": "The sludge was initially clarified by centrifugation for 30 min at 8,000 rpm (10,400   g) with a Sorvall RC-2B centrifuge (DuPont- Sorvall, Wilmington, Del.)."
    },
    {
      "paragraph_index": 17,
      "comment": "Samples were stored frozen at  -20oC until use."
    },
    {
      "paragraph_index": 18,
      "comment": "Thawed samples were then centrifuged for 30 min at 18,000 rpm (39,000   g)."
    },
    {
      "paragraph_index": 19,
      "comment": "The resulting liquid was neutralized to pH 7.0 with 1 M HCl and then prefiltered through a 0.8- m-pore-size Supor-800 membrane filter (Gelman Sciences, Ann Arbor, Mich.)."
    },
    {
      "paragraph_index": 20,
      "comment": "The SS was then purged with N2 and filter sterilized in an anaerobic chamber through a double 0.8-0.2- m-pore-size Acrodisc PF filter (Gelman) into sterile vials."
    },
    {
      "paragraph_index": 21,
      "comment": "In some instances, the SS was lyophilized in a Labconco LYPH   LOCK 4.5-liter Freeze Dry system, model 77510 (Labconco Corporation, Kansas City, Mo.). Preliminary tests showed that lyophilized SS performed as well as SS."
    },
    {
      "paragraph_index": 22,
      "comment": "The SS contained 75 mg of organic carbon per liter and  0.05 mM acetate or other volatile fatty acids."
    },
    {
      "paragraph_index": 23,
      "comment": ""
    }
  ]
}